## Context
Raid 2026-10-27: on PR 1798 the codex seat refused NOT-RUN (no read tool, git forbidden) and was re-run with the files
inlined; on PRs 1806 and 1795 codex seats had no shell or temp dir, so their clears were code reads, not runs. The
review records still counted them as seats.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The codex door's seat rails give read access to the review tree consistently; a seat that cannot read reports NOT-RUN, never a clear.
- [ ] A seat's status line says whether it ran tests or read code only.
- [ ] The harness gate passes.
